# Code owners for Argus.
#
# Matching is last-rule-wins, so the catch-all comes first and the narrower
# rules below override it. Every rule resolves to the same person today; they
# are written separately because the paths differ in blast radius, and a second
# maintainer should be able to take ownership of source without silently
# inheriting the pipeline that signs and publishes executables.
#
# This file requests review automatically. It only *blocks* a merge if the
# branch ruleset also requires code-owner approval.

# Everything.
*                       @malopezr7

# The release pipeline: compiles Hermes and publishes binaries users download
# and execute. Changes here alter what lands on someone else's machine.
/.github/               @malopezr7
/scripts/               @malopezr7

# The result channel. A defect here can make a failing suite report as passing.
/packages/framework/    @malopezr7

# Pure domain and ports. Anything impure landing here breaks the architecture.
/packages/core/         @malopezr7
